 they will uh with dialogue options  you know give you  context if you would like it or give you  a quest and you go on your merry way it  basically feels a lot more like an rpg  than the first game did and i think that  that probably ties pretty directly into  the um news articles recently concerning  the play time uh where it came out  because they tweeted i guess uh  they came out with it that uh it would  take you 500 hours to finish the full  game when i asked the dev said that it  would only take 20 hours to finish the  main campaign which seems pretty  reasonable to me i feel like even the  first dying light i don't remember how  long it took me to finish but it was  lengthy enough but i would think that  the um  500 hours comes from you know 100  completing the map finding everything  and also from the side quests being a  lot beefier and the game as as a whole  just being a lot more rpg like  across the board it's a big map um very  very vertical actually is one thing that  uh they've definitely improved upon from  the first game it's a really really  vertical map basically with a whole  bunch of characters for you to talk to  quests for you to get context for you to  learn again it's almost like you  combined something a lot more fallout  with dying light uh and i do want to be  clear that that i liked that i found  that pretty fun but that does not  take away  from the  dying light of it all it is still very  uh focused on the free running or  parkour and what i would describe is  like very brutal in your face  kind of vicious  combat some of the narrative choices  definitely do seem dramatic um and i was  definitely interested in the story and  and the relationships and the characters  and and what was going on with them yeah  i really want to play more of it where  the story is concerned i never knew if i  was really making the right choice you  know i had an option to like abandon  someone or go help someone and i didn't  i didn't know what to do it wa